[options]         
[A.]
                                        <h2>Attack on Nimbus~.<a href="#mission22">~[IfortGump.46]</a></h2>
                                    ~[IedgeFarm.43]
<br>                                                                                  ~1~y<?!{sw_difficulty1}>HARD</?><?{sw_difficulty1}>EASIER</?>~.<br>
After you and the {sw_god5} beat the Furies in the 10 year tournament you asked the {sw_god5} if you could return to your homeland of Nimbus.<br>
The Nimbians were invaded before the tournament started and you want to go provide them with help.<br>
{swgod5}: <i>"I will allow you to go home!"</i><br>
you: ~I"Really? Oh, thank you Lord {sw_god5}!"~.<br>
{sw_god5}: <i>"However, you won't be providing help. Instead, you need to attack
 them while they are still rebuilding. Your sole purpose for this attack is to kill
 2 priests. Sure, you can kill all of them, but I only need the King and his Special
 Protector dead."<br>
"So, go! Go now before I boil your blood on my altar."</i> 
$Button=More,Tell,A1

[A1]
                                                      <h2>Attack on Nimbus~.<a href="#mission22">~[IfortGump.46]</a></h2>
                                                  ~[IedgeFarm.43]
<p>
While you are floating above Nimbus you spot an easy position to attack. You notice that
 the 2 guards barely have their temple built. During the night you silently float down
 into Nimbus. You have just enough time to allow your Golems to bridge to one of the guards
 island and plant some weapons near him.
<p>
                           ~kJust before dawn - You start your Attack on Nimbus.~.
<p>
            <a href="cmd:ShowTechnology,55"> ~[IfortGump.50] </a>                                                  <a href="cmd:DoNothing,0">~[IfortGump.22] </a>                                            <a href="cmd:Tell,guideHades.overview">~[Ipriest.13]</a><br>
<a href="cmd:ShowTechnology,55">Review Knowledge</a>                            <a href="cmd:DoNothing,0">Enter Hades Realm</a>                    <a href="cmd:Tell,guideHades.overview">I'm too Scared!</a>
$OnExit= ,PlaySound,golemMove1.wav
$Button= ,Tell,A.

<$PlaySound,somethingCreated.wav>


